            <div xml:id="d749">

                <pb facs="0773" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/664: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-11T20:00:00+09:00">December 11,
                            1939—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 11—8:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>676. The Counselor of the French Embassy recently informed a member of my staff
                    in confidence that sometime ago the Foreign Office proposed that the French
                    Government permit the stationing in Indo-China of Japanese officials to
                    “control” the traffic toward China with a view to preventing the shipment of
                    arms. This was refused.</p>
                <p>A second proposal has just been made by the Foreign Office that an official of
                    the Foreign Office who has been handling Indo-Chinese affairs accompanied by a
                    Japanese military officer be sent on a mission to Hanoi for a few days “to
                    inform the Japanese Consul General concerning the general situation”. The
                    military officer would “assist in explaining the military operations in
                    Kwangsi”. The Foreign Office also suggested that there would be no objection to
                    the French Military Attaché at Tokyo accompanying the mission.</p>
                <p>The French Ambassador has referred the matter to Paris but has received no
                    reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
